Camoufox: the content-reachable file set must match a stock Firefox release.

Twelve chrome/resource packages are flagged contentaccessible=yes, so any page
can load their files as subresources and a file Camoufox adds or drops there is
a one-line build tell. Two diverged from stock 152.0.4, both measured from a
content page:

  chrome://global/content/crashes.{html,js,css} were absent, because
  --disable-crashreporter strips them in toolkit/crashreporter/jar.mn. The
  JAR_MANIFESTS entry is outside that moz.build guard, so shipping the three
  content files does not build or enable the crash reporter.

  chrome://browser/content/browser-development-helpers.js was present, because
  it is gated #ifndef MOZILLA_OFFICIAL and Camoufox is not an official build.
  Its presence is a positive "built from source" tell. Two other places reach
  it -- browser-main.js loads the script, and BrowserComponents.manifest
  registers DevelopmentHelpers.init as a browser-window-delayed-startup
  category entry (browser-init.js called it directly before Firefox 156) -- so
  dropping the file from the package alone breaks _delayedStartup, which must
  reach its "browser-delayed-startup-finished" notification because juggler's
  newPage awaits exactly that. Both call sites go with the file.

Setting MOZILLA_OFFICIAL=1 would fix the second one at the source, but it also
moves telemetry, update-channel and branding defaults that Camoufox sets
deliberately, so the narrower change is here.

Guard: tests/patches/contentaccessible-parity.py.

diff --git a/browser/base/content/browser-main.js b/browser/base/content/browser-main.js
index f7f364290e..9d9be0eb33 100644
--- a/browser/base/content/browser-main.js
+++ b/browser/base/content/browser-main.js
@@ -11,9 +11,6 @@
   if (AppConstants.MOZ_DATA_REPORTING) {
     Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/browser-data-submission-info-bar.js", this);
   }
-  if (!AppConstants.MOZILLA_OFFICIAL) {
-    Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/browser-development-helpers.js", this);
-  }
   Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/browser-pageActions.js", this);
   Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", this);
   Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/browser-customtitlebar.js", this);
